---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CHAPTERS, PARTS } from '../lib/chapters';

const writtenCount = CHAPTERS.filter((c) => c.written).length;
---
<Base>
  <div class="narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="tagline">$ mine --everything<span class="cursor">▊</span></p>
    <h1>Blockchain, from the <em>hash</em> up.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Strip away the hype and a blockchain is three things: hashes chaining history,
      signatures proving ownership, and proof-of-work making forgery expensive. This
      course builds all three, breaks each naive version, and ends with a chain you
      mined, tampered with, and defended.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href="/chapters/01-what-is-blockchain/">Start Chapter 1 →</a>
  </section>

  <h2 class="section-title" id="how">How this works</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">Every chapter follows the same promise:</p>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>01</span>Start below the abstraction</h3>
      <p>Before "invest in crypto", we answer "what is a block, physically?"</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>02</span>Break it to learn it</h3>
      <p>Tamper with the chain, double-spend a coin — then see the defense.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>03</span>Build the real thing</h3>
      <p>Mining, signatures, Merkle trees — all stdlib Python, all runnable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-card">
      <h3><span>04</span>The giants become readable</h3>
      <p>Bitcoin's UTXO and Ethereum's contracts mapped onto your toy chain.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title" id="chapters">Chapters</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">
    {writtenCount} of {CHAPTERS.length} chapters fully written{writtenCount === CHAPTERS.length ? ' — every chapter, start to finish.' : ' — the rest are outlined and on the way.'}
  </p>
  {PARTS.map((part) => (
    <div>
      <p class="part-label">{part}</p>
      <div class="chapter-grid">
        {CHAPTERS.filter((c) => c.part === part).map((c) => (
          <a class="chapter-card" href={`/chapters/${c.slug}/`}>
            <span class="num">{String(c.order).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <span class="body">
              <span class="t">{c.title}</span>
              <span class="b">{c.blurb}</span>
            </span>
            <span class="status dim">{c.written ? '✅' : '📝'}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}
  </div>
</Base>
